# SheetJS publishes xlsx on npm only through 0.18.5; Trivy's fixed 0.19.x/0.20.x
# versions are not available from the npm registry. Keep this narrow until the
# web XLSX viewer migrates off the abandoned package.
CVE-2023-30533
CVE-2024-22363

# CVE-2026-14257 has no compatible fix for brace-expansion 1.x.
# The remaining 1.x paths come from legacy build tools that require minimatch 3.
# Keep this exception until those upstream tools remove the minimatch 3 paths.
CVE-2026-14257

# The sandbox runtime intentionally grants its isolated agent root access for
# package installation and system-level development tasks.
AVD-DS-0002

# GHSA-86w9-cpqp-85rv: node-forge <= 1.4.0 accepts extra nested DigestAlgorithm
# elements in RSA PKCS#1 v1.5 signature VERIFICATION. No patched release exists
# (1.4.0 is the latest). The only runtime use is the sandbox egress-shim CA
# (apps/kortix-sandbox-agent-server/src/services/egress-shim/ca.ts), which
# generates keys and signs certificates and never verifies an RSA signature.
# apps/web lists the package but imports nothing from it. Remove when fixed upstream.
CVE-2026-85393

# DS-0010 (RUN using sudo): only apps/sandbox/Dockerfile uses sudo. Those stages
# run as the sandbox user, which has passwordless sudo by design (same reason as
# AVD-DS-0002 above); hadolint DL3004 carries the same documented exception.
AVD-DS-0010

# CVE-2026-93687 (braces 3.0.3, DoS on deeply nested patterns): no fixed release
# exists. The one runtime path is @daytonaio/sdk -> fast-glob, used only by
# Image.extractCopySources (Dockerfile COPY globbing); apps/api never builds a
# Daytona Image from a Dockerfile or local files. Every other path is lint, dev,
# or build tooling. Remove when a fixed braces ships.
CVE-2026-93687

# CVE-2026-93748 (http-cache-semantics 4.2.0, max-stale disclosure): no fixed
# release exists. Reached only through Electron build tooling (@electron/get,
# electron-builder, node-gyp) and the docs-site build (blume/astro), never in a
# server request path. Remove when a fixed release ships.
CVE-2026-93748
